{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-21): P0 resolved — the deterministic CI import-walk is APPROVED in place of the LLM import-integrity criterion. No LLM criterion will be built (same grounds as the P3 rejection: deterministically measurable classes get deterministic checks). Task 8b86-fe08 (the standalone import-integrity criterion proposal) is being closed as declined with this ruling; a new task for the deterministic import walk (full importlib walk of rebar.* in the wheel-probe venv + a scripts/ import leg, with a local non-CI invocation for portability) is being filed and dispatched. With this, all of P0-P3 are adjudicated: P0 deterministic-walk, P1 pending FP assessment, P2 approved/minimal-value, P3 rejected, ci-gate-compat rejected."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787356466477016001,"uuid":"2fbad301-3916-452e-ba85-bbce3fad1b07"}